cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, cite it as below. The author block is left neutral while the manuscript is under double-blind review and is completed at acceptance."
title: "84-cell solvability diagnosis of vocational cybersecurity exercises under AI assistance: reproduction artifact"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-19"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Data, harness and analysis scripts for a diagnosis of exercise validity under AI
  assistance. Fourteen containerised capture-the-flag exercises are crossed with three
  variants (original, paraphrase, patched safe) and two information levels (interface
  names shown, URL only), giving an 84-cell matrix. The artifact contains every agent
  run and per-round record behind the reported rates, the exercise definitions, the
  evaluation harness, and a script that recomputes all 65 reported quantities from the
  data with no external dependencies.
keywords:
  - assessment validity
  - AI solvability
  - capture-the-flag
  - vocational education
  - reproducible evaluation
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous (author block completed at acceptance)"
